course: dictionary
lesson: 1097
title: Two meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives brainless two: an informal, rude meaning for stupid, and a meaning for having no brain. The context, the words around it, tells you which one is right.
explain: «In SpongeBob SquarePants, Patrick Star is famously brainless.» Here the word is an insult used as a joke. Patrick is not a real starfish with no brain. The show is making fun of how silly he is, so brainless means stupid.
explain: Now read this: «A real starfish has no brain at all.» This time brainless means having no brain, which is a fact about the animal. Ask yourself: is the sentence describing a silly person, or a living thing? The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning to use.
fact: Brainless has two main meanings: stupid, not thinking at all (informal and rude), and having no brain.
fact: In everyday speech, brainless is an insult, so it can hurt someone's feelings.
fact: Jellyfish and sponges are brainless animals: they have no brain, yet they still survive.
fact: A brainless plan is a silly plan, one that nobody should have made.
fact: A real starfish has no brain at all, yet it walks on hundreds of tube feet.
exercise: «In SpongeBob SquarePants, Patrick Star is famously brainless.» In this sentence, what does brainless mean? | Covered in shells | *Stupid, a rude joke about how silly he is | Having a very big brain | Able to swim very fast
exercise: Which of these is a brainless animal, meaning it has no brain? | A dog that loves to run | A teacher with a big book | *A sponge | A clever parrot
exercise: Jayden says, «Your plan is brainless.» What does he mean? | It is made of wood | It is a very clever plan | It has a brain drawn on it | *It is a silly plan
test: «A real starfish has no brain at all, yet it walks on hundreds of tube feet.» What does brainless mean in that sentence? | Very fast | *Having no brain | Sleepy | Stupid
test: Why should you be careful about saying «brainless» to a friend? | Because it means happy | *Because it is a rude insult in everyday speech | Because it only describes plants | Because it is a long word
exam: Which is the best way to find out which meaning of brainless is right? | *Read the words around it to see if the sentence is about a person or an animal | Pick the longest meaning and use it | Ask the nearest person without reading the sentence | Guess the first meaning you see every time
